% class decides. Each wrapper in this directory supplies the appearance.

\booktitle{John}
\chapternumber{1}

\s1{The Beginning}
\r{(Genesis 1:1–2; Hebrews 11:1–3)}

\v{1}In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was
God.
\v{2}He was with God in the beginning.
\v{3}Through Him all things were made, and without Him nothing was made that has
been made.
\v{4}In Him was life, and that life was the light of men.
\v{5}The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not
overcome\fn{1:5 Or \em{comprehended}} it.\par

\s1{The Witness of John}

\v{6}There came a man who was sent from God. His name was John.
\v{7}He came as a witness to testify about the Light, so that through him everyone
might believe.
\v{8}He himself was not the Light, but he came to testify about the Light.
\v{9}The true Light, who gives light to everyone, was coming into the world.
\v{10}He was in the world, and though the world was made through Him, the world did
not recognize Him.
\v{11}He came to His own, and His own did not receive Him.
\v{12}But to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the
right to become children of God—
\v{13}children born not of blood, nor of the desire or will of man, but born of
God.\par

\s1{The Word Became Flesh}
\r{(Psalms 84:1–12)}

\v{14}The Word became flesh and made His dwelling among us.\fn{1:14 Or \em{and
tabernacled among us}} We have seen His glory, the glory of the one and only
Son\fn{1:14 Or \em{the Only Begotten} or \em{the Unique One}} from the Father, full
of grace and truth.
\v{15}John testified concerning Him. He cried out, saying, “This is He of whom I
said, ‘He who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’”
\v{16}From His fullness we have all received grace upon grace.
\v{17}For the law was given through Moses; grace and truth came through Jesus
Christ.
\v{18}No one has ever seen God, but the one and only Son, who is Himself God
and\fn{1:18 Or \em{but the only begotten God, who}; BYZ and TR \em{but the only
begotten Son, who}} is at the Father’s side,\fn{1:18 Greek \em{in the Father’s
bosom}} has made Him known.\par

\s1{The Mission of John the Baptist}
\r{(Isaiah 40:1–5; Matthew 3:1–12; Mark 1:1–8; Luke 3:1–20)}

\v{19}And this was John’s testimony when the Jews of Jerusalem sent priests and
Levites to ask him, “Who are you?”
\v{20}He did not refuse to confess, but openly declared, “I am not the Christ.”
\v{21}“Then who are you?” they inquired. “Are you Elijah?”\xref{1:21 Mal. 4:5; Matt.
11:14} He said, “I am not.” “Are you the Prophet?” He answered, “No.”
\v{22}So they said to him, “Who are you? We need an answer for those who sent us.
What do you say about yourself?”
\v{23}John replied in the words of Isaiah the prophet:\par

\q1{“I am a voice of one calling in the wilderness,}
\q2{‘Make straight the way for the Lord.’”\fn{1:23 Isaiah 40:3 (see also LXX)}}

\noindent\v{24}Then the Pharisees who had been sent
\v{25}asked him, “Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah,
nor the Prophet?”
\v{26}“I baptize with\fn{1:26 Or \em{in}; also in verse 31 and twice in 33} water,”
John replied, “but among you stands One you do not know.
\v{27}He is the One who comes after me, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy
to untie.”
\v{28}All this happened at Bethany beyond the Jordan, where John was baptizing.\par

\s1{Jesus the Lamb of God}
\r{(Matthew 3:13–17; Mark 1:9–11; Luke 3:21–22)}

\v{29}The next day John saw Jesus coming toward him and said, “Look, the Lamb of
God, who takes away the sin of the world!
\v{30}This is He of whom I said, ‘A man who comes after me has surpassed me because
He was before me.’
\v{31}I myself did not know Him, but the reason I came baptizing with water was that
He might be revealed to Israel.”
\v{32}Then John testified, “I saw the Spirit descending from heaven like a dove and
resting on Him.
\v{33}I myself did not know Him, but the One who sent me to baptize with water told
me, ‘The man on whom you see the Spirit descend and rest is He who will baptize with
the Holy Spirit.’
\v{34}I have seen and testified that this is the Son of God.\fn{1:34 SBL \em{the
Chosen One of God}}”\par

\s1{The First Disciples}
\r{(Matthew 4:18–22; Mark 1:16–20; Luke 5:1–11)}

\v{35}The next day John was there again with two of his disciples.
\v{36}When he saw Jesus walking by, he said, “Look, the Lamb of God!”
\v{37}And when the two disciples heard him say this, they followed Jesus.
\v{38}Jesus turned and saw them following. “What do you want?” He asked. They said
to Him, “Rabbi” (which means Teacher), “where are You staying?”
\v{39}“Come and see,” He replied. So they went and saw where He was staying, and
spent that day with Him. It was about the tenth hour.\par
